{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a large +10.6pp gain over singleprofile (config_001, 0.485 acc), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is the most impactful design choice so far. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the RNA side is where the signal lives. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further improve over the simple avgpool, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal for this data. This experiment (config_003) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002—only the aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer—so any performance difference is directly attributable to the aggregation strategy. Why it is the best next step: (1) it resolves a fundamental structural question that will inform every subsequent multiprofile and multimodal experiment (e.g., configs 020/021/026/027 all use transformer aggregation); (2) if transformer helps, it justifies investing in transformer-based multimodal configs; if it does not, we can prune that axis and focus budget on encoder choice or fusion strategy; (3) it stays within the well-characterized RNA-only space where signal is strong, making the result interpretable rather than confounded by the weak image modality."
}

